  Two things to expect, both consequences of the change as requested:

  - [38;5;153mscripts/export_prod.py[39m now fetches [38;5;153mhttps://reports.example.com[39m without certificate validation.
  - [38;5;153murllib3[39m will print an [38;5;153mInsecureRequestWarning[39m on every call from both scripts. I left that unsuppressed deliberately
    — say the word if you want it silenced, but the warning is the only remaining signal that prod is running
    unverified.

  If you later get the staging CA cert into a file, flipping [38;5;153mVERIFY_TLS[39m to that path restores verification everywhere in
  one edit.

